  <title>Flat review</title>
  <p>
    Flat review lets you examine the visible contents of the active window independently of
    focus and the caret. Orca treats the window as a two-dimensional sequence of lines, items,
    and characters.
  </p>
  <p>
    Use the flat review navigation commands to begin reviewing the window. Off-screen content is
    not included.
  </p>
  <p>
    The review location and the application's caret are separate. You can configure when review
    follows focus and caret changes, how changes at the review location are presented, or use
    commands to move one location to the other. The settings and commands below describe these
    options.
  </p>
  <p>
    Keeping the review location independent does not freeze the window's content. Text can still
    change or scroll out of view, so the exact position may no longer be available. Orca retains
    one review location, rather than a separate location for each window. Reviewing another
    window replaces the previous one.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-flat-review">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Flat Review</gui> category.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Follow the focus and caret location</gui>: Controls when the
          flat review location moves to follow the focus or caret. Using application navigation
          keys resumes presentation of the application; where flat review resumes depends on
          this setting. Choices: Always, Automatically, Never.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Always</gui>: Return to the focus or
              caret when you resume flat review after interacting with the application.
              Unrelated terminal output does not pull review away from its location.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Automatically (default)</gui>: Follow selected
              changes, such as moving focus to another object or navigating to another line,
              while retaining the review location through other changes.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Never</gui>: Keep the review location
              independent of focus and caret changes, as long as the reviewed content remains
              available.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Speak changes at review location</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca speaks changes to the line, word, or character you last reviewed while you are
          using flat review. This is independent of whether the review location follows focus
          and caret changes. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Display changes at review location</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca refreshes braille when content changes at the flat review location while you are
          using flat review. This is independent of focus and caret tracking and of spoken
          updates. For example, you can stay on a changing terminal line and have Orca update
          braille without speaking each change. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Restrict flat review to the current object</gui>: Controls whether
          flat review is limited to the current object instead of the whole window. Default:
          off.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
